  "body": "From the review of PR #190 (#130). The default cylinder stock takes its diameter from the footprint's diagonal, so a round part of radius R gets a bar of radius about 1.41R. Since #130, the turning kernels rough from the bar's OD, so every auto-fitted lathe setup now cuts many passes in air and its program changes.\n\nDone means: an auto-fitted lathe (or mill-turn) cylinder stock takes the part's revolved max radius about the spindle axis plus the stock allowance, not the XY diagonal. Pin: a round part's auto stock radius is R + allowance. Note the change for existing projects that kept an auto stock.",
